This lab exercise in the Digital Logic course exposed me to creating digital logic circuits, generating truth tables, and visualizing them with timing diagrams using the Deeds Simulator. 
Going through the process of designing and simulating a combinational circuit helped me understand how circuits behave and how their inputs affect outputs. 
The hands-on approach made it easier to grasp these concepts and gave me a better understanding of the steps involved in digital circuit design and simulation. 
Overall, this exercise reinforced the theoretical knowledge while providing a practical experience of working with digital circuits.
